WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.001 --> 00:00:15.163
on instinct, Zann rubbed his hands together.

2
00:00:15.183 --> 00:00:19.145
"Decelerate!" Zann immediately felt himself slow down.

3
00:00:19.965 --> 00:00:22.647
Soon he was drifting down no faster than a leaf.

4
00:00:23.487 --> 00:00:28.650
"It's a good thing we just got tested on deceleration in Safety Spells class," he thought as he

5
00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:30.211
landed gently on the palace roof.

6
00:00:32.064 --> 00:00:34.025
"Zann!" someone shouted from far overhead.

7
00:00:34.726 --> 00:00:37.507
Zann's friends were still trying to evade the wild dragons.

8
00:00:38.248 --> 00:00:42.970
Fala was attempting to steer her dragon closer to him, but the thunder chargers kept blocking her.

9
00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:48.234
"Go!" Zann shouted, using a Sound-Shifting spell to carry his words to her.

10
00:00:48.254 --> 00:00:49.915
"It's too risky.

11
00:00:50.535 --> 00:00:51.976
I'll meet you back in the woods!"

12
00:00:51.996 --> 00:00:53.717
"Are you sure?"

13
00:00:54.057 --> 00:00:56.298
Fala sent her words back to Zann the same way.

14
00:00:57.019 --> 00:00:59.668
Zann nodded and gave her a thumbs-up.

15
00:00:59.688 --> 00:01:02.691
Fala and Darb steered the cloud gliders back toward the forest.

16
00:01:03.431 --> 00:01:07.675
The wild dragons chased them for a while and then stopped, disappearing into the clouds.

17
00:01:08.495 --> 00:01:12.078
Knowing that his friends were safe, Zann looked around for a way into the palace.

18
00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.501
He was standing on the apex of a steep roof.

19
00:01:16.222 --> 00:01:19.624
Looking down he could see the top of a small dormer jutting out.

20
00:01:19.644 --> 00:01:22.987
"Maybe there's a window on that dormer," he thought.

21
00:01:23.788 --> 00:01:28.672
Zann was nervous about using any more magic than he needed to—especially with Morb so close.

22
00:01:29.436 --> 00:01:33.417
Keeping himself as flat as he could, he inched his way down slowly.

23
00:01:34.197 --> 00:01:36.898
When Zann was about halfway down, he lost his grip.

24
00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:38.779
"Oh no!"

25
00:01:39.119 --> 00:01:40.519
he cried, sliding fast.

26
00:01:41.279 --> 00:01:43.700
Zann could see the edge of the roof quickly getting closer.

27
00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:47.141
He slid past the dormer and then he was in midair.

28
00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:50.442
Zann cried out, "Decelerate—" Bam!

29
00:01:52.082 --> 00:01:55.623
"Ouch!" Zann looked at the small balcony he'd just landed on.

30
00:01:56.263 --> 00:01:57.144
Then he saw the door.

31
00:01:57.464 --> 00:02:00.761
With a sigh of relief, he got up and headed into the palace.

32
00:02:01.902 --> 00:02:05.363
Morb and Slib walked down the cracked steps of the ancient staircase.

33
00:02:05.383 --> 00:02:07.944
"This is what you call a dungeon?"

34
00:02:08.344 --> 00:02:11.046
said Morb, wrinkling his nose at the awful smell.

35
00:02:11.946 --> 00:02:12.707
Slib bowed.

36
00:02:13.247 --> 00:02:15.148
"Forgive me, Your Highness.

37
00:02:16.108 --> 00:02:18.689
It hasn't been used since the Old Times."

38
00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:21.511
The place was a mess.

39
00:02:22.171 --> 00:02:27.866
The stone walls were cracked and crumbling, many of the iron bars were either missing or badly rusted,

40
00:02:28.226 --> 00:02:30.868
and everything was coated in a thick layer of dust.

41
00:02:30.888 --> 00:02:38.954
"A few Voids have already arrived in response to your invitation," Slib went on in that servile tone

42
00:02:38.994 --> 00:02:40.715
that Morb already found annoying.

43
00:02:41.515 --> 00:02:45.458
"Perhaps we could put them to work cleaning and repairing this place."

44
00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:47.679
Morb shot him a sharp look.

45
00:02:47.699 --> 00:02:50.661
"Is that all you think Voids are good for?"

46
00:02:51.042 --> 00:02:51.602
he demanded.

47
00:02:51.622 --> 00:02:54.184
"Cleaning up others' messes?"

48
00:02:55.204 --> 00:02:56.484
Slib looked confused.

49
00:02:56.504 --> 00:03:00.666
"I only meant—" Morb didn't let him finish.

50
00:03:00.686 --> 00:03:03.766
"How many Reds have turned themselves in so far?"

51
00:03:04.647 --> 00:03:06.867
Slib's expression changed to nervousness.

52
00:03:06.887 --> 00:03:09.688
"Uh "How many?"

53
00:03:10.508 --> 00:03:13.209
"None, Your Majesty," Slib said.

54
00:03:13.229 --> 00:03:16.410
"But that's typical of Reds, isn't it?

55
00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:20.691
Always thinking they're too good to follow the rules."

56
00:03:21.672 --> 00:03:22.892
Morb gnashed his teeth.

57
00:03:24.036 --> 00:03:27.899
He was so furious that he almost struck Slib down with a Blast spell.

58
00:03:27.919 --> 00:03:31.161
"Never mind," Morb muttered.

59
00:03:31.181 --> 00:03:33.042
"Soon it won't matter."

60
00:03:33.062 --> 00:03:35.704
"Pardon me, Your Majesty?"

61
00:03:36.144 --> 00:03:36.645
said Slib.

62
00:03:37.305 --> 00:03:38.246
Morb glanced at him.

63
00:03:38.626 --> 00:03:40.127
"Stand back," he ordered.

64
00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:43.729
Touching his fingertips together, Morb pointed at the dungeon.

65
00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:47.172
The walls quickly rebuilt themselves out of the rubble.

66
00:03:48.888 --> 00:03:53.792
Strong iron bars grew out of the hard stone floor and formed new cell doors.

67
00:03:54.632 --> 00:03:55.953
Slib gasped.

68
00:03:55.973 --> 00:03:57.134
"Your Majesty!"

69
00:03:57.494 --> 00:03:58.075
he exclaimed.

70
00:03:58.095 --> 00:04:00.136
"Such power!"

71
00:04:01.017 --> 00:04:01.817
Morb ignored him.

72
00:04:02.518 --> 00:04:06.580
Closing his eyes, he summoned up the energy for a much more difficult task.

73
00:04:07.181 --> 00:04:10.143
"Come to me," he murmured.

74
00:04:10.963 --> 00:04:17.228
Zap! In a flash all the Red prisoners from the fortress appeared in the cells.

75
00:04:18.076 --> 00:04:23.798
Morb hardly heard Slib's exclamations this time, or the cries of the surprised prisoners either.

76
00:04:24.579 --> 00:04:28.920
He'd used up much of his energy last night, and this task had drained him again.

77
00:04:29.681 --> 00:04:31.922
He would need another magic infusion soon.

78
00:04:31.942 --> 00:04:40.205
"Slib," he ordered hoarsely, holding onto a pillar for support, "tell the trolls to bring more leeches immediately."

79
00:04:41.606 --> 00:04:42.406
Slib gulped.

80
00:04:42.426 --> 00:04:47.368
"Your Highness," he said, "there aren't many leeches left.

81
00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.321
You used most of them last night."

82
00:04:50.341 --> 00:04:53.682
"Just bring them to me," commanded Morb.

83
00:04:54.342 --> 00:04:59.483
In order to restore himself the night before, Morb had been forced to use almost all of his

84
00:04:59.563 --> 00:05:01.504
leeches on the non-Reds in the palace.

85
00:05:02.344 --> 00:05:06.245
As soon as the old woman arrived with his sea sponge, he would have to send her out

86
00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:07.165
for more leeches.

87
00:05:07.185 --> 00:05:09.826
"Are you okay, little buddy?"

88
00:05:10.146 --> 00:05:13.167
Darb asked, peeling Zing loose from the cloud glider's back.

89
00:05:13.907 --> 00:05:17.828
The fire whistler had been hanging on for dear life the whole way back to the forest.

90
00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:20.281
"Never mind him," Perda said.

91
00:05:20.301 --> 00:05:21.502
"What about Zann?"

92
00:05:22.242 --> 00:05:23.783
Fala slid down from her dragon.

93
00:05:23.803 --> 00:05:26.325
"He told us to go," she said.

94
00:05:26.345 --> 00:05:30.107
"We never would have gotten past those thunder chargers anyway.

95
00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:34.150
Zann can take care of himself—he'll get out of the palace."

96
00:05:35.111 --> 00:05:36.091
Perda glanced around.

97
00:05:36.111 --> 00:05:37.632
"How will he find us?

98
00:05:38.453 --> 00:05:40.474
We must be miles from where we started.

99
00:05:41.194 --> 00:05:43.416
Maybe we should fly back to the original spot."

100
00:05:44.096 --> 00:05:49.058
But one look at the exhausted cloud gliders told Perda that that wasn't practical right now.

101
00:05:49.078 --> 00:05:51.899
"We should at least send him a message moth."

102
00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:53.260
"Good idea."

103
00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:55.621
Fala snapped her fingers to summon a moth.

104
00:05:56.421 --> 00:05:58.362
After scribbling a message, she released it.

105
00:05:59.122 --> 00:06:01.383
It was midday by now, and it was getting hot.

106
00:06:02.484 --> 00:06:05.905
Perda wandered toward a shadier spot with the others trailing behind her.

107
00:06:06.725 --> 00:06:11.187
Suddenly Perda felt magical energy surround her as she was lifted into the air.

108
00:06:11.207 --> 00:06:13.681
"Hey!" she shouted.

109
00:06:14.121 --> 00:06:16.303
She struggled against the magic, but it was useless.

110
00:06:17.063 --> 00:06:19.085
She could see that her friends were being lifted as well.

111
00:06:19.105 --> 00:06:24.089
"Do not try to resist," a voice commanded from somewhere in the forest.

112
00:06:24.109 --> 00:06:26.051
"You're surrounded."
